Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Needle Kisses The Ore
- Story & Context: Silas the scavenger finds a glowing fragment of a comet in the local shipyard, an object so hot it burns his fingerprints away as he embeds it into his favorite cello. The sound begins as a low, mechanical moan echoing through the hollowed-out hulls of decommissioned tankers, signaling the end of the long silence. "The sky fell down and it’s singing my name."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a human hand stitching a piece of glowing, violet meteorite into the wooden bridge of an antique cello, metallic dust floating in a spotlight of cold blue light, poetic and gritty.

Track 2: Suture The Swing
- Story & Context: Clara sits in her darkened attic studio, laboriously cutting apart old records to "fix" the broken melody of her grandmother’s favorite jazz hit by stitching in rhythmic samples of her own failing heartbeat. She confesses to the gear-cogs that she is only doing this because the silence of the city has become a physical weight she can no longer carry alone. "Every seam is a promise we broke to the sun."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A young woman with sharp, angular features sitting at a workbench covered in tangled gold clockwork gears and magnetic tape ribbons, her reflection in a broken mirror looking like an unfinished mannequin.

Track 3: The Pendulum’s Mercy
- Story & Context: In the wake of the city’s collapse, the citizens gather at the Grand Archive to witness the final performance of the Clockwork Menders as they destroy their instruments to prevent the gravity-shifted music from further tearing the reality of their streets. The last note played is so discordant it shatters every glass window in the square, leaving the survivors in a profound, ringing stillness that defines their new, post-history life. "We unraveled the light to find what stayed hidden."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A towering, rusted iron pendulum swinging through the center of a crowded, ruined urban plaza, people standing in silence watching the clockwork mechanisms disintegrate into falling sparks, cinematic and melancholic.

